  "slug": "max-consecutive-ones-iii",
  "title": "Max Consecutive Ones III",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "variable-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "this is Longest Repeating Character Replacement in disguise - what if '1' were the letter you're trying to extend, and '0' were the letter you're allowed to replace up to k times?",
    "grow the window to the right, keeping a running count of zeroes inside it",
    "if the zero count ever exceeds k, shrink from the left until it's back to at most k, updating the count as you go",
    "the window never needs to shrink below its previous best length, so you're really just tracking the widest window that was ever valid"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "recounting zeroes in the window from scratch instead of maintaining a running count",
    "shrinking the window more than necessary once it's valid again",
    "off-by-one when computing the window length from its left and right boundaries"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a binary array `nums` (only 0s and 1s) and a number `k`. You\nmay flip up to `k` of the 0s to 1s.\n\n**Return the length of the longest stretch of consecutive 1s you can create.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10^5",
      "nums[i] is either 0 or 1",
      "0 <= k <= nums.length"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "k = 0 (no flips allowed, answer is the longest existing run of 1s)",
      "k is large enough to flip every 0 in the array",
      "the array is already all 1s"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
